# What is tracked, and why the exclusions below are what they are.
#
# TRACKED: notebooks/*.ipynb (a clone is unreadable without them), src/*.py, spec/, scripts/,
# tests/ and requirements.txt.
#
# THE TRACKED NOTEBOOKS ARE INTERNAL RUN RECORDS. They declare PUBLIC_NOTEBOOK = False and hold
# the stored output of the internal run, which is what makes them worth reading. They are not
# publication-ready. A public copy is a SEPARATE file written by
# scripts/make_public_notebooks.py, which declares the flag True and retains stored output only
# in the cells spec/public_notebook_cells.json names explicitly; every other cell is cleared.
#
# NOT TRACKED: anything that resolves or holds cohort data, anything a run produced, and
# anything local to one machine. MCS Sweep 6 is UKDS Safeguarded Tier 1a and git history does
# not forget, so the rule is to exclude by default and add deliberately.

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# Editor, OS and assistant state
.DS_Store
.claude/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Patch machinery. Backups and temporary siblings written beside a notebook while an edit is
# applied; none belongs in history.
*.before_*
*.patch_tmp
*.internal_flag_tmp
*.wording_tmp

# Configured locations. `paths.json` names the restricted data roots on one machine; ship an
# example instead of the real file.
src/paths.json

# Run products. Everything a run generates is written below $THESIS_WORK_DIR, so none of these
# names should ever appear here. They are ignored anyway, with no exception for any file type:
# a figure or a LaTeX fragment is a generated result like any other, and an exception is what
# lets one back in. Candidates await disclosure review and are never repository files.
outputs/
publication_outputs/
publication_candidates/

# Cohort data, fitted models and person-level scores. Restricted by licence and by grain.
data/
models/
scores/
tests/

# Environments
.env
.venv/
venv/

